[[Open This|SDLC]]

---


The ''Software Development Life Cycle'' (SDLC) is a structured, iterative framework used by development teams to plan, design, build, test, and deploy high-quality software efficiently. It acts as a roadmap to reduce risks, manage complexity, and ensure the final product meets customer requirements within budget. Key stages include planning, requirements analysis, design, coding, testing, deployment, and maintenance.